<article class="post" data-controller="reveal" id="painting_<%= painting.dom_key %>">
  <%= render "shared/plate", painting: painting, eager: painting_counter < 2,
        describedby: nil, resting: "This work is resting." %>

  <%# The action rail (story 0020) — Keep alone. Locals: kept_ids (required,
      not defaulted — see below).

      No Zoom: unlike `daily/_day.html.erb`'s rail, the plate above is already
      the zoom trigger here (`shared/_plate.html.erb:7`, and both `/feed` and
      `/artists/:slug` already mount `shared/_zoom`), so a second control for
      the same action would be a duplicate tab stop.

      No count: mark-only on multi-work surfaces (`decisions/0010`, narrowed
      2026-08-19) — see `favorites/_control.html.erb` for why.

      Rendered INLINE, not as a fetching frame with `src`: `/feed` and
      `/artists/:slug` are walled and private
      (`test/integration/public_cache_headers_test.rb`), so the constraint
      that forces `/`'s eager-frame-plus-placeholder split — a public,
      shared-cached page cannot carry a live `button_to` — does not apply
      here. The mark is correct in the first paint; there is no fetch and so
      no loading state to design for.

      Unconditional, unlike `_day`'s. This partial has no preview mode, and
      the plate above never hides its own zoom trigger without also hiding
      the rail — the two states that make `_day`'s wrapper conditional don't
      exist here, so there is no state in which this rail would be empty. A
      resting work (no image) is still a work you can keep. %>
  <div class="rail">
    <%= render "favorites/control", painting: painting,
          kept: kept_ids.include?(painting.id), autofocus: false, compact: true %>
  </div>

  <div class="label">
    <h2 class="label__title <%= "label__title--long" if painting.long_title? %>"><%= painting.title %></h2>
    <%# `show_artist:` default true. The artist page passes false — the name
        already carries the h1 there, and rendering it again under every work
        would repeat it once per work (design review D2). %>
    <%= render "shared/artist_line", painting: painting if local_assigns.fetch(:show_artist, true) %>
    <% if painting.meta_line.present? %>
      <p class="label__meta"><%= painting.meta_line %></p>
    <% end %>

    <% if painting.description.present? %>
      <div class="label__body" data-controller="expand">
        <p class="label__text" data-expand-target="text"><%= painting.description %></p>
        <button type="button" class="label__more" data-expand-target="button" data-action="expand#toggle" hidden>More</button>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <p class="label__credit"><%= painting.credit_line %></p>
  </div>
</article>
